    rdfs:label "Evidence for Bristles used in Hat-Making, Brushes, Upholstery & Turnery: P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 63"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "BRISTLES: the strong glossy hairs on the back of the hog, used by brushmakers, saddlers, shoemakers, and others. Those from the wild boars of Russia are most esteemed."@en ;
